# Claude Code governance wiring, the same class as the Cursor entries above:
# regenerated per clone by the session bootstrap, machine-local, never repository
# content. `.claude/settings.json` is tracked and deliberately not listed here.
.claude/hooks/
.claude/rules
.claude/skills/
.mcp.json

# This repository is npm-only: `package-lock.json` is the committed lockfile and
# every workflow runs `npm ci`. A pnpm lockfile appearing in a working tree is a
# tooling artifact, and committing one would introduce a second, unverified
# dependency resolution. Delete this line if pnpm ever becomes a supported path.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# L4 local-autonomy runtime state (machine-local; never repository content).
# `.l9/` itself is a governed namespace — `.l9/meta-authority.yaml` and
# `.l9/metadata-index.jsonl` are meant to be committed — so only this subtree is ignored.
.l9/autonomy/
